WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.576
(hooves on pavement)

00:00:03.576 --> 00:00:06.648
- The horses really do
help you with aggression.

00:00:06.648 --> 00:00:08.800
Once you own a horse, and you out,

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.688
that's all your mind is on, is having fun.

00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:15.688
My Shahir and I'm a Concrete Cowboy.

00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:23.660
(hooves on pavement)

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.827
I first got a horse after I turned 10.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.263
I was young so I was
like, "I like that horse."

00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:35.096
I thought it was cool.

00:00:36.407 --> 00:00:38.247
Horses have a temper just like us.

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:41.663
Me and Shadow had to combine
out tempers and work together

00:00:41.663 --> 00:00:44.047
because she used to walk while
everybody else was running,

00:00:44.047 --> 00:00:45.792
buck, throw people off,

00:00:45.792 --> 00:00:47.095
and I used to always get back on her,

00:00:47.095 --> 00:00:49.591
just to have the patience.

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:52.787
When I ride people actually
give me like props,

00:00:52.787 --> 00:00:56.796
they actually applaud me,
the hood guys and everything.

00:00:56.796 --> 00:00:58.238
They be asking me, can I ride?

00:00:58.238 --> 00:00:59.253
You wanna trade?

00:00:59.253 --> 00:01:00.428
People like it.

00:01:00.428 --> 00:01:02.195
- Hello horsey.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.028
Hello.

00:01:10.785 --> 00:01:13.299
- When the stable started
about 10 years ago,

00:01:13.299 --> 00:01:15.549
it gave me something to do.

00:01:18.271 --> 00:01:21.995
Something to keep the kids
busy with, keep them occupied

00:01:21.995 --> 00:01:23.011
from running the street,

00:01:23.011 --> 00:01:24.594
getting in trouble.

00:01:28.043 --> 00:01:30.965
In Southwest Philadelphia there's
a lot of senseless killing

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:34.346
and I try to give kids
something to get away

00:01:34.346 --> 00:01:35.521
from stuff like that.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.851
And when they start
learning with the animals,

00:01:37.851 --> 00:01:41.305
they kinda calm down, because
they teaching, they learning,

00:01:41.305 --> 00:01:43.638
and it helps them out a lot.

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:50.809
- Hey, hey, hey.

00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:52.233
Violence in this community is crazy.

00:01:52.233 --> 00:01:56.400
I done lost a brother, a
uncle, I lost a lot of friends,

00:01:58.867 --> 00:02:01.866
but when I work with the horses
it's like a type of therapy.

00:02:01.866 --> 00:02:04.441
I can have fun and not
worry about everything else

00:02:04.441 --> 00:02:06.608
that's going on around us.

00:02:07.545 --> 00:02:10.202
If I would have never met
Malik and sat around horses,

00:02:10.202 --> 00:02:12.297
I probably would have been doing stuff

00:02:12.297 --> 00:02:13.401
that I wasn't suppose to be doing.

00:02:13.401 --> 00:02:14.763
Getting in trouble.

00:02:14.763 --> 00:02:16.649
Once you get to running and having fun,

00:02:16.649 --> 00:02:19.732
it seems like all that is forgotten.

